Package: ldapkg
Type: Package
Title: Predictive Linear Discriminant Analysis with an R6 Interface
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Abdoul", "Ouedraogo", email = "ouedraogoabdoulfaisal47@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Author: Abdoul Ouedraogo [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Abdoul Ouedraogo <ouedraogoabdoulfaisal47@gmail.com>
Description: Predictive linear discriminant analysis (LDA) for a categorical
    target with two or more classes. The computational core relies on
    sufficient statistics (class means, within-class and total scatter
    matrices) and Cholesky factorisations. The package returns the
    classification functions, class posterior probabilities, Wilks' lambda
    with Rao's F approximation, partial Wilks' lambda for each explanatory
    variable, canonical discriminant axes, resubstitution and cross-validated
    error rates, and stepwise variable selection (forward, backward,
    stepwise) in which categorical predictors are handled as blocks of dummy
    variables. A Shiny application illustrating all features is included.
